Baseline

1. base
Training script:
  d-2GPU-1hr-refc_value-base-refc_input-no_hydrometeors-finer_graph_v1-single_input-202405.sh
Config:
  training/docs/user-guide/examples/anemoi-training-rrfs-lam-neural-lam-static-forcing-202405-1h-refc-value-base-refc-input-no-hydrometeors-finer-graph-v1-single-input.yaml
Goal:
  One-month GraphTransformer baseline with refc as input/output and hydrometeors removed.
Key setup:
  - one-month May 2024 window
  - GraphTransformer, finer_graph_v1, single input
  - refc input/output
  - hydrometeors removed
  - base weights: refc=20, range_weight_factors=[1,2,2,4]
  - normalization: landcover none, orography none, swdown mean-std
  - model.num_channels=1024

Derived Tests

2. base_1
Training script:
  d-2GPU-1hr-refc_value-base_1-refc_input-no_hydrometeors-finer_graph_v1-single_input-202405.sh
Config:
  training/docs/user-guide/examples/anemoi-training-rrfs-lam-neural-lam-static-forcing-202405-1h-refc-value-base_1-refc-input-no-hydrometeors-finer-graph-v1-single-input.yaml
Goal:
  Test whether static/forcing normalization was causing the ocean artifact and poor updates.
Differences from base:
  - normalization changed to:
    - landcover none
    - orography max
    - swdown none
  - everything else intended to stay the same

3. base_1 one-day reduced-vars
Training script:
  d-2GPU-1hr-refc_input-graphtransformer-base_1-finer_graph_v1-single_input-day20240505-pl925500-reduced_vars-202405.sh
Config:
  training/docs/user-guide/examples/anemoi-training-rrfs-lam-neural-lam-static-forcing-202405-1h-refc-input-graphtransformer-base_1-finer-graph-v1-single-input-day20240505-pl925500-reduced-vars.yaml
Goal:
  Isolate same-day behavior on an easier case and check whether base_1 normalization resolves the fixed ocean artifact.
Differences from base:
  - training restricted to 2024-05-05 only
  - reduced variable layout: pl925500 reduced-vars
  - smaller model width: num_channels=512
  - still refc input/output
  - still base_1 normalization

4. base_1 one-month reduced-vars
Training script:
  d-2GPU-1hr-refc_input-graphtransformer-base_1-finer_graph_v1-single_input-1month202405-pl925500-reduced_vars.sh
Config:
  training/docs/user-guide/examples/anemoi-training-rrfs-lam-neural-lam-static-forcing-202405-1h-refc-input-graphtransformer-base_1-finer-graph-v1-single-input-1month202405-pl925500-reduced-vars.yaml
Goal:
  Separate time-window effects from variable-layout effects by keeping the reduced pl925500 layout but training over the broader May 2024 period.
Differences from base:
  - reduced variable layout: pl925500 reduced-vars
  - smaller model width: num_channels=512
  - base_1 normalization
  - same broad May 2024 window idea as base

5. base_2
Training script:
  d-2GPU-1hr-refc_value-base_2-refc_input-no_hydrometeors-finer_graph_v1-single_input-202405.sh
Config:
  training/docs/user-guide/examples/anemoi-training-rrfs-lam-neural-lam-static-forcing-202405-1h-refc-value-base_2-refc-input-no-hydrometeors-finer-graph-v1-single-input.yaml
Goal:
  Test the model-capacity hypothesis for the one-month refc-input / no-hydrometeors setup.
Differences from base:
  - inherits base_1 normalization
  - model.num_channels increased from 1024 to 2048

6. diffusion base_1 no-refc-input
Training script:
  d-2GPU-1hr-refc_value-no_refc_input-diffusion-base_1-finer_graph_v1-202405.sh
Config:
  training/docs/user-guide/examples/anemoi-training-rrfs-lam-neural-lam-static-forcing-202405-1h-refc-value-loss-no-refc-input-diffusion-base_1-finer-graph-v1.yaml
Goal:
  Test whether diffusion helps compared with deterministic regression when refc is not part of the input state.
Differences from base:
  - diffusion model/task instead of GraphTransformer forecast model
  - refc is output-only, not input
  - base_1 normalization
  - hydrometeor-dropping aligned later in this branch

7. diffusion base_1 refc-input no-hydrometeors
Training script:
  d-2GPU-1hr-refc_value-base_1-refc_input-no_hydrometeors-diffusion-finer_graph_v1-202405.sh
Config:
  training/docs/user-guide/examples/anemoi-training-rrfs-lam-neural-lam-static-forcing-202405-1h-refc-value-base_1-refc-input-no-hydrometeors-diffusion-finer-graph-v1.yaml
Goal:
  Test diffusion with the same refc-input / no-hydrometeors idea as the deterministic base_1 setup.
Differences from base:
  - diffusion model/task instead of deterministic GraphTransformer
  - base_1 normalization
  - hydrometeors removed

Interpretation Notes

- The key dimensions being tested are:
  - normalization: base vs base_1
  - time window: one-day vs one-month
  - variable layout: reduced-vars vs no-hydrometeors full-ish layout
  - architecture/task: GraphTransformer vs diffusion
  - capacity: base_1 (1024) vs base_2 (2048)

- The main diagnostic question behind the recent additions is:
  whether the one-month failures come mainly from
  1) broader training window,
  2) larger variable/output layout,
  3) insufficient model capacity,
  or 4) a genuinely poor checkpoint/training trajectory.
